# A whole number widens to a decimal wherever the two have to agree: the two
# sides of `+`, an argument, the branches of an `if` or a `match`, and the items
# of a list. A decimal never narrows by itself; `round`, `floor` and `truncate`
# say how.
plus = program(a, b) do a + b done
whole = floor(3.7)
flag = true

print(plus(whole, 2.5));
print(if flag then whole else 2.5 done);
print([whole, 2.5]);
print(whole < 3.5)
